    schema:description "At Jellyfish, we believe in the power of diverse perspectives and inclusive collaboration. We welcome individuals who excel in collaborative, varied teams and value the unique contributions that each person brings to the table. Jellyfish is a global digital marketing agency; a unique fusion of tech enthusiasts, creative minds, and media and data experts all united to empower our clients along their digital journey. Our commitment to embracing diverse perspectives fuels our innovation and strategies that challenge the status quo, reinvent media activation, and craft influential stories for our global clients and their customers. Join us in shaping a future where business growth and personal fulfilment go hand in hand. Job Description Reporting to a Client Partner, you will act as a coordinator between our French clients and our specialist teams, assisting with communication to ensure the smooth running of campaign delivery projects. As part of a fast-paced team of Client Partners, Media Planners, Analysts, and Campaign Activators your support will be essential to the growth and retention of our key clients. Responsibilities Assist the Client Partners in tracking the project pipeline, helping to flag upcoming needs to the wider team. Help collect information from various client teams to assist in the processing of briefs. Support the team in tracking budget approvals and monitoring campaign spend, helping to flag any discrepancies or changes. Set up regular project status meetings. You will be responsible for taking minutes, capturing \"next steps\", and ensuring all project \"watch outs\" are documented. Assist in the preparation and editing of presentations. Support with client reporting and tracking of deliverables Develop a deep understanding of our portfolio of services and our integrated marketing offering to eventually identify our clients' needs and how we can fulfil them. Qualifications You're able to sign an internship agreement for a full-time, 6+ month commitment (Monday through Friday). You're fluent in French and have a conversational level of English. You have some client-facing experience through an internship, apprenticeship or a personal project. You have an interest in social media, digital marketing or online advertising, and AI. You're good at adapting strategies and plans to navigate unforeseen circumstances. You embrace challenges as opportunities and seek feedback to enhance your skills. You love getting to know your clients, developing long-lasting relationships and adding value to their business. Note: We emphasise skills, expertise and behavioural attributes over years of experience and traditional degrees. If you want to join our collaborative team, we invite you to apply today with your resume in English. Additional Information Join Jellyfish and experience a workplace where we prioritise your growth, celebrate your contributions, and empower you to tailor your work environment to suit your needs. 💫 Custom Work Environment: Work remotely for up to 60% of your days and shape your day between 8am. and 6:30pm with flexible working hours. Unfortunately, there has been an increase in fake recruiters impersonating Jellyfish and unlawfully using our brand name. If you are unsure if an email with a job offer you have received is genuinely from Jellyfish, or if you suspect any fraudulent activity, please report it to • €1.1K – €1.5K per month Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow" ;
