t you’ll do Partner with the team to deliver high-priority initiatives integrating our Salesforce instance with Angi's new unified platform in the US market Contribute to, uphold, and help evolve the team's development quality standards and Salesforce best practices Ground your work in the data and context behind key decisions Be an active voice in product and technical discussions Apply your expertise and experience to support the other senior team members as they make and implement critical technical decisions over the coming months Who you are You possess deep knowledge of Salesforce application architecture and software design principles You have 8+ years of commercial experience developing in LWC and Apex, including automated testing You use Visual Studio Code (or similar IDE), Git and AI tooling in your development workflow, and are experienced with Salesforce code deployments using CI/CD tools You are a collaborative communicator and have experience working in agile and lean environments on cross functional teams. You have Platform Developer I & II certifications Nice to have Additional Salesforce core platform certifications (e.g., Service Cloud, Experience Cloud) System Architect or Certified Technical Architect certification Trailhead badges or superbadges (Apex Specialist, Lightning Web Components Specialist) Familiarity with automated testing philosophy: TDD, Apex tests, Jest tests Benefits The salary band for this position ranges from €85,000 - €105,000 (annualized), commensurate with experience and qualifications Hybrid work environment and home office set-up allowance Temporary work from abroad policy Regular team and social events Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
